WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.183
Welcome back! You've announced a change and

00:00:04.183 --> 00:00:08.560
you're met with silence or subtle resistance.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:09.953
What's going on?

00:00:09.953 --> 00:00:16.220
Resistance to change is rarely about the change itself. It's often about

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:20.530
what people fear they will lose. Certainty,

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:24.640
competency, or connection. An agile coach

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:30.520
doesn't just push their agenda. They first diagnose the root of the resistance. Your

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:37.680
job is to listen for the unspoken fears so you can address them directly.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.856
A manager was rolling out a new software and

00:00:40.856 --> 00:00:43.960
her team was dragging their feet instead of

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.250
pushing harder. She held one-on-ones and asked,

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.400
what is the biggest concern for you with this

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:56.038
new system? She discovered they weren't resistant to the software.

00:00:56.038 --> 00:00:58.600
They were afraid they wouldn't

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:05.160
be able to learn it fast enough and would look incompetent. The problem wasn't the

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:08.943
change. It was fear about losing competence.

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:12.640
Your play is to listen for the loss and the

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:17.540
stress points. Think of a recent change you've implemented.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:20.280
What did your team stand to lose?

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.718
Certainty, competency, or connection.

00:01:22.718 --> 00:01:25.880
Where are the stress signals? What steps can you

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.027
take to anticipate and mitigate them?

00:01:29.027 --> 00:01:33.960
Understanding this will change how you lead. You need your

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.300
player to take on a challenge of a new role,

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:40.640
but they seem hesitant. How can you use this

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.601
diagnostic lens to uncover their underlying

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:46.700
fear and coach them through it? Your playbook

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.051
has a coaching through hesitation guide.

00:01:50.051 --> 00:01:53.820
Use it to diagnose questions and prepare your

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.763
conversation and uncover the root cause.

00:01:56.763 --> 00:02:00.220
Once you can diagnose resistance, the next step

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:04.900
is to coach for agility. We'll cover that in our final segment.
